Production 44e7e36b, the sampled minute at 98% busy with twenty candidates:
`sortedLevels feed.js:60 19%` was the top frame of the main thread. The feed
sorted each side of every book with M.cmp per comparison four to six times per
applied message (truncate, checksum, snapshot). Now sortAndTruncate sorts each
side once, with the double of each price as the sort key (monotonic rounding;
equal doubles fall to the exact comparator; a price failing the guard sends the
side down M.cmp) and the one sorted, truncated array is shared by truncation,
checksum and snapshot. Same order, CRC and digest, byte for byte — proven on a
real feed through a snapshot and two hundred random updates.

execution/*.js re-pinned (§4.45); judge and watch unchanged.

